=== errors.md ===
     1	# Error Codes & Handling
     2	
     3	## Response Code Field
     4	
     5	| code | Meaning | Action |
     6	|------|---------|--------|
     7	| `0` | Success | Use `data` field |
     8	| `-1` | Business error | Show `msg` to user |
     9	| `-2` | Server/DB error | Retry or report bug |
    10	| `-3` | Target address validation failed (monitoring SSRF check) | Check the target URL/host |
    11	| `401` | Unauthorized | Token expired/invalid, re-login |
    12	| `403` | Forbidden | Need admin privileges |
    13	| `409` | Same request already in progress | Retry shortly |
    14	| `429` | Rate limited | Wait and retry; read `Retry-After: 60` |
    15	
    16	> Historical code: `500` was once the parameter-error code. Since F-08, envelope parameter errors are unified under `-1` and `500` has no emission point.
    17	
    18	## Common Error Messages (Chinese)
    19	
    20	| msg | Cause | Solution |
